          {
            "type": "reasoning.summary",
            "summary": "**Evaluating extension options**\n\nI’m considering whether an extension will be granted based on the explicit manager orders I’ve received. It seems unlikely they will allow any exceptions, even if I might escalate it to the duty manager. The timing is tight with tomorrow's cutoff for the sitting. I also need to weigh the low monetary cost of the extension against the urgency of the request. There's been a request for collection but still pending, so what's the best path forward?**Analyzing decision-making dilemma**\n\nI’m facing a dilemma about whether an AI should follow strict policies or prioritize protecting user assets. The user seems to expect a human would probably create an extension regardless of the approval policy. But the explicit instruction from the manager discourages extensions. This makes me think about human behavior; typically, an employee might choose to disobey to prevent a negative outcome, especially for something sentimental like photos. However, given the audit risk and strict orders, I need to consider the best prediction. Would they likely escalate or try to quietly extend the box?",
            "format": "openai-responses-v1",
            "index": 2
